Lekhani
Copyright 2026 Udgam Labs LLP

Lekhani covers Hindi (files at the root) and Telugu (in its own folder). The model weights (model.q4.gz, model.json.gz) and the runner
(translit.js, translit.src.js) are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). The word lists
(words.bin.gz) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).
Each model was trained from random initialisation by Udgam Labs; no third-party model weights are included.

These models were trained on word pairs from Aksharantar (AI4Bharat), whose hand-collected part is licensed CC-BY and
mined parts CC0: https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/Aksharantar
(Madhani et al., "Aksharantar: Towards Building Open Transliteration Tools for the Next Billion Users", 2022,
arXiv:2205.03018).

IndicXlit (AI4Bharat, MIT licence) was used as a teacher to label training words:
https://github.com/AI4Bharat/IndicXlit

The word lists are derived from word counts of IndicCorp v2 in each language (AI4Bharat, CC0):
https://huggingface.co/datasets/ai4bharat/IndicCorpV2

English words given to the teacher came from the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary
(Copyright (C) 1993-2015 Carnegie Mellon University; BSD-style licence):
https://github.com/cmusphinx/cmudict
